    &=\sqrt{\det\left(G\left(d\left(\varphi^{-1}\circ\psi\right)_{\varphi^{-1}}\left(\bm\varepsilon_1\circ\varphi^{-1}\right),\dots,d\left(\varphi^{-1}\circ\psi\right)_{\varphi^{-1}}\left(\bm\varepsilon_n\circ\varphi^{-1}\right)\right)\right)}
    \\[4 mm]
    &=\left|\det\left(d\left(\varphi^{-1}\circ\psi\right)_{\varphi^{-1}}\right)\right|\sqrt{\det\left(G\left(\bm\varepsilon_1\circ\varphi^{-1},\dots,\bm\varepsilon_n\circ\varphi^{-1}\right)\right)}
    \\[4 mm]
    &=\left.\left|\det\left(d\left(\varphi^{-1}\circ\psi\right)_{\psi^{-1}}\right)\right|\right|_{\psi\circ\varphi^{-1}}\left.\sqrt{\det\left(G\left(\bm\varepsilon_1\circ\psi^{-1},\dots,\bm\varepsilon_n\circ\psi^{-1}\right)\right)}\right|_{\psi\circ\varphi^{-1}}
    \\[4 mm]
    &=\left.\left|\det\left(J_\varphi^\psi\circ\psi^{-1}\right)\right|\right|_{\psi\circ\varphi^{-1}}\left.\sqrt{\det\nolimits_\psi(g)}\right|_{\psi\circ\varphi^{-1}}=\left.\left(\left|\det\left(J_\varphi^\psi\circ\psi^{-1}\right)\right|\sqrt{\det\nolimits_\psi(g)}\right)\right|_{\psi\circ\varphi^{-1}}
\end{align*}
Thus, for some (measure) density denoted by $\left|\partial x/\partial y\right|$, the integral representation of $\mathrm{Vol}\left(\Omega\right)$ with respect to the chart $(\mathcal{U},\varphi)$ can be rewritten as such, and then compared to the representation relative to $(\mathcal R,\psi)$:
\begin{align*}
    &\int_{\mathcal{U}}\sqrt{\det\nolimits_\varphi(g)}\,d^nx=\int_\mathcal{U}\left.\left(\left|\det\left(J_\varphi^\psi\circ\psi^{-1}\right)\right|\sqrt{\det\nolimits_\psi(g)}\right)\right|_{\psi\circ\varphi^{-1}}d^nx=\int_\mathcal R\left|\det\left(J_\varphi^\psi\circ\psi^{-1}\right)\right|\sqrt{\det\nolimits_\psi(g)}\left|\frac{\partial x}{\partial y}\right|d^n y
