Heuristically, the differential $d^nx=\left|\partial x/\partial y\right|d^ny$. Therefore, given any integrable function $f:\mathcal{U}\to\mathbb{R}$ of the specific form $\sqrt{\det\nolimits_\varphi(g)}$, for any such metric $g$, the following change of variables procedure can be executed: 
